  {
    "episode_id": 72784,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72784.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "What's difficult from the industry standpoint is 50 different laws. I think the industry was willing to accept and that's what we came to an agreement about on the floor. uh... some sort of a phased-in approach uh... as long as it was you know it didn't have a patchwork of fifty different state laws but what we're headed for right now with uh... individual states implementing their own main toy laws which course by the way it per month uh... they've exempted dairy because that's our home state industry it's uh... there you know they want to stick it to everybody else but uh... i think you just have to then you'd have to have uh... you know food manufacturer processor somewhere that's uh... It's moving, if you're moving product across state lines, you're dealing with all these different regimes labeling regimes and that's going to pose an enormous amount of cost on them trying to get their products to the marketplace. So I think that's in the end, you know, what the hang up is and it's a cost issue and it's a cost ultimately that gets passed on. to consumers and its American families are going to pay the price for this.",
