    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 72784,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72784.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Well, that's true. And that's why we basically concluded that an immediate mandatory label, you know, if we went to an immediate one today, it would be perceived as an indicator that food products made with GMO ingredients are somehow not safe. And that is simply not true. You know, as I said, if foods made with GMO ingredients have been proven safe by sound scientific and research, we need that technology if we're going to feed the planet And so it's unfortunately, that's the perception that that creates. And that's why you asked earlier about going to a mandatory label. If that happened immediately, that's the perception that you would create out there is that somehow these ingredients are not safe. And so we got to avoid that. And it does stigmatize it and creates a a false impression in the minds of American people when it comes to the things that we put on the shelves in our grocery stores and supermarkets. So this has got to be fixed. Like I said, we put a",
