    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "Well, no. I mean, it's because this was a negotiated and agreed to. I mean, the Farm Bill was, you know, I think it's hardly dry about a year ago. We got finally a new Farm Bill in place. And if you're going to continually come in and raid Farm Bill programs to try and fund other areas of the government. Then, you know, what that means, essentially, is that you basically are reopening the farm bill. You've got settled law. Law that's put in place is designed to provide predictability and certainty for people who have to make decisions when it comes to planting and their farming operations. And then, all of a sudden, you're changing the rules in the middle of the game. So, it's not a function. And it's not a good part. And we know this program works. It's been retooled, refined, savings have been achieved, there have been cuts and in crop insurance programs, but the time to do that is when we're debating the farm bill,",
