  {
    "episode_id": 72784,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72784.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "well i think that the uh... You know, it's going to be very challenging. It always isn't an election. You get to give a number of years. You're going to have an election. And of course, every four, you're going to have a presidential election. And we're already in the midst of that. So I think it will make it difficult, challenging, to try and get a budget done this year. But we're going to make every effort that we can. We think it's important that we assure the American people that we're going to follow regular order. We did agree to some top-line numbers last year. And I hope that the Senate moves forward and not only with a budget process, but making some improvements to the budget process. I've been a big advocate for a long time going back to my days in the House of Representatives that we need to reform the budget process in this country because it's a dysfunctional process. It doesn't work. And the reason that we end up most years with an omnibus spending bill or a continuing resolution to fund government is because the budget process is broken and dysfunctional. And so I'm hoping that not only uh... do you know that this let lead us to a budget this year but also support reforms that but i think a critical if we're going to get a a budget process that actually works for the american people and actually helps control uh... the growth in federal standing which is essential if we're going to keep from bankrupting the country and in passing on a mountain at the future generations",
