    "turn_idx": 35,
    "turn_text": "Well, I do. I think these are what he perceives to be legacy issues for him. I think it's going to be a paper thin legacy because many of these things could be reversed by a future president. And in many are being overturned by the courts. I mean, the president has had numerous of these what I would characterize as regulatory overreach attempts rebuffed by the courts in this country. Whether it's the Waters United States rule, his so-called Clean Power Plan, or what I think more accurately is a national energy tax. And his attempt to try and use recess appointments to pack the National Labor Relations Board, the court ruled 9-0 against the president on that. So, you know, this president is somebody who wants to use executive power to achieve an agenda and create a legacy, but I don't think it's going to be a legacy that's doable. And, frankly, certainly not one that's good for the American people, but I suspect that in the waning days of this administration they'll do everything they",
